A||N||11||86SEFIERO||6x9 speakers in stock dash speaker locations||||1||
Z||000000||86SEFIERO||06-22-2000||05:03 AM||||<BR>Has any body tried this? How did they fit? And How did you mount them?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||06-22-2000||05:26 AM||||I would recommend installing a good set of separates. 4”ers with tweeters mounted on a 4x10 plate. The sound is far superior than the 6x9 or 4x10. ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-22-2000||11:07 AM||||Definitely separates.  A round speaker will give you better sound than an oval one will.  (Sound waves are round.  I'm almost beginning to sound smart <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  Too bad this info is from someone else.)  You can fit some tweeters in the small section of your side vents.  I've seen it done.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||06-22-2000||11:07 AM||||Yeah,the 4"ers are the better way,also,you can aim the tweeters in a way that'll make it sound like you're standing in a very large theatre,or concert hall.You aim them at an angle,towards the windshield,so that the sound bounces off the glass and heads towards the opposite side of the car.<BR>Right speaker focused towards drivers right ear,left speaker towards passengers' left ear.<BR>A small pice of plumbers tape,or sheet metal will make for quick adjustments.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||06-22-2000||12:55 PM||||I haven't taken my smart pill today.  Anyone have pics of this arrangement?||||reg||5
Z||000005||lowCG||06-22-2000||05:13 PM||||My old car had this arrangement,my current car just has some funky oval speakers.The tweeters go towards the outboard side of the speaker opening,and as close as possible to the underside of the grills.The curvature of the windshield helps as a parabolic reflector.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||06-22-2000||08:44 PM||||I did! You CAN'T beat the sound from a top quality 6x9 versus ANY 4x10! I had them in my first Fiero(85 2M4)5 years ago and didn't hesitate to put them in when I got my 87GT! I'm waiting for DaRkLoRD to add the directions link to my website and I'll post when he's done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 06-22-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||Black88GT||06-22-2000||11:40 PM||||6x9s will fit, but they look VERY disproportional in that location. To me, they just don't look right. If I ever had time, I would work on my planned speaker project, which is 6 1/2" Component speakers where the 4x10s go.  4" components provide good sound, but NO BASS AT ALL.  6 1/2" have better sound and way better bass.  The only problem is that it is harder then the 4", you can buy an adapter plate for the 4" so its like a straight drop in replacement.  I am still trying to figure out the easiest way to go about my installation...||||reg||3
Z||000008||Gokart||06-23-2000||05:37 AM||||I had to do a small amount of trimming around the speaker opening where the 4x10's sit that is TOTALLY unoticeable once the grills are back on! The passenger side speaker goes under the dash and is held in with cable ties and the drivers side wedges in over the top and is held in the same way. Nothing disproportional about it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||06-23-2000||05:43 AM||||As hard as it is to find a perfect Feiro dash.....Trimming is NOT an option for me.....Go with the 4"ers & tweeters.||||reg||14
Z||000010||Monkeyman||06-23-2000||10:13 AM||||Try 5 1/4"ers.  The only trimming you have to do (I measured) is to the inner lip where the speakers rest.  You can put both of them in from the top, too.  Mount your tweeters wherever you feel, but most will fit in the bottom (smaller of the two) side vent.  I've seen them mounted 2 different ways in the vents.  WT III has the larger mount and he has them mounted to the outside of the vent.  I saw one just the other day that had the smaller mount and he just made a couple small boxes.  Mounted the tweeters in the boxes, then mounted the boxes *inside* the vents.  He popped the vent back in place and you can not tell that there are any speakers there.  That's stealth <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">!  (BTW--I could see what he was doing because he only had one side done.  I don't have Xray vision.  At least I don't think I do.)||||reg||1
Z||000011||lowCG||06-23-2000||10:15 AM||||Some 6 1/2" speakers in the doors would fix things up,haven't even looked at this possibility; anyone done this?||||reg||1
